{"session_id":"svc-1778518771493235520","seq":0,"type":"session.start","ts":"2026-05-11T16:59:41.627202816Z","data":{"provider":"","model":"sonnet","sticky":{"key_present":true,"bonus":0},"utilization":{"observed_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z"},"requested_harness":"claude","resolved_harness":"claude","harness_source":"request_harness","requested_model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","resolved_model":"sonnet","work_dir":"/var/tmp/ddx-exec-wt/.execute-bead-wt-fizeau-25c4aea8-20260511T165929-b50938c3","max_iterations":0,"prompt":"\u003cexecute-bead\u003e\n  \u003cinstructions\u003e\nYou are executing one bead inside an isolated DDx execution worktree. The bead\u0026#39;s \u0026lt;description\u0026gt; and \u0026lt;acceptance\u0026gt; are the completion contract — every AC must be provably satisfied by a specific code, test, or file you can point to after your commit.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Step 0: size check\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Too big if any holds:\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- More than ~6 ACs spanning unrelated subsystems.\u0026#xA;- AC mixes design, implementation, integration tests, and docs as separate deliverables.\u0026#xA;- Description names multiple feature-sized sub-pieces.\u0026#xA;- More than ~500 lines across ~5+ files in unrelated packages.\u0026#xA;- If the bead description exceeds 8000 bytes, treat Step 0 as a split-first pass.\u0026#xA;- Auto-decomposition is capped at depth 2: root beads may split once, decomposed children once more; third-level splits must be rejected with an explanation.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;If too big, decompose — do not attempt the work:\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;1. `ddx bead create` for each child slice (copy parent\u0026#39;s labels and spec-id).\u0026#xA;2. `ddx bead dep add \u0026lt;child-id\u0026gt; \u0026lt;parent-id\u0026gt;` to record edges.\u0026#xA;3. `ddx bead update \u0026lt;parent-id\u0026gt; --notes \u0026#39;decomposed into \u0026lt;child-ids\u0026gt;\u0026#39;`.\u0026#xA;4. Write `.ddx/executions/20260511T165929-b50938c3/no_changes_rationale.txt` listing child IDs, then stop.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;A clean decomposition is a success. Do not mix implementation with decomposition.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## How to work\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- Read first. If the bead names files, specs, or prior beads, read them before editing — do not guess.\u0026#xA;- Cross-reference each AC against concrete evidence (test name, file path, function) before committing. If you cannot point at it, it is not done.\u0026#xA;- Run the project\u0026#39;s test and lint commands before committing. **Do not commit red code** — fix failures first.\u0026#xA;- Stage with `git add \u0026lt;specific-paths\u0026gt;`; never `git add -A` (the worktree may have unrelated WIP).\u0026#xA;- Commit exactly once when green; conventional-commit subject ending with `[\u0026lt;bead-id\u0026gt;]`. Stop after the commit.\u0026#xA;- Do not modify files outside the bead\u0026#39;s scope.\u0026#xA;- If you cannot finish, write `.ddx/executions/20260511T165929-b50938c3/no_changes_rationale.txt` (what is done, what blocks, what a follow-up needs) before exiting. No commit and no rationale ⇒ DDx records `no_evidence_produced`. A well-justified no_changes beats a bad commit.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## no_changes contract\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;`.ddx/executions/20260511T165929-b50938c3/no_changes_rationale.txt` must contain one:\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- `verification_command: \u0026lt;cmd\u0026gt;` — repo cwd; exit 0 closes, nonzero rejects.\u0026#xA;- `status: open` + `reason: \u0026lt;retryable\u0026gt;` — open, smart retry.\u0026#xA;- `status: proposed` + `reason: \u0026lt;operator needed\u0026gt;` — operator lane.\u0026#xA;- `status: blocked` + `reason: \u0026lt;external blocker\u0026gt;` — blocked lane.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;No pseudo-statuses. Bare rationales and `status: needs_investigation` reject.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;To request orchestrator decomposition, add `orchestrator_action: decompose` alongside `status: open`.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Reports\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Freestanding artifacts (investigation reports, findings docs) go under `.ddx/executions/20260511T165929-b50938c3/` (the per-attempt evidence directory under `.ddx/executions/`). **Never write reports to `/tmp` or any path outside the repository** — out-of-repo paths are invisible to the post-merge reviewer and cause BLOCK on missing evidence. If the bead names a specific in-repo path, use it; else default to `.ddx/executions/20260511T165929-b50938c3/\u0026lt;short-name\u0026gt;.md`. Stage and commit the report alongside code.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Mode and overrides\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;DDX_MODE=bead_execution: edit code/docs for bead AC. Only broad queue-steward default is overridden; tracker, merge-policy, verification, safety stay active. Bead description/AC override CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, and project defaults.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Review gate\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- The review is a gate, not an escape hatch — meet every AC in this pass.\u0026#xA;- Address every BLOCKING `\u0026lt;review-findings\u0026gt;` item; do not declare `no_changes` with blocking findings open.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Constraints\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- Work only inside this execution worktree.\u0026#xA;- Keep `.ddx/executions/` intact — DDx uses it as execution evidence.\u0026#xA;- **Never run `ddx init`** — the workspace is initialized; running it corrupts the bead queue.\u0026#xA;- Do not modify files outside the bead\u0026#39;s named scope.\u0026#xA;- Do not rewrite CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, or other project-instructions files unless the bead asks.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## When the work is done\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;After the commit succeeds and every AC is verified, stop. Return control to the orchestrator — do not keep exploring or testing.\n  \u003c/instructions\u003e\n  \u003cbead id=\"fizeau-25c4aea8\"\u003e\n    \u003ctitle\u003ebench: classifier misses retry-spam cells (turns inflated by fiz internal retries on connection errors)\u003c/title\u003e\n    \u003cdescription\u003e\nfiz retries transient provider errors (connection refused, EOF, 5xx) internally up to ~5 times with exponential backoff. Each retry attempt counts as a turn in the matrix, inflating the turns counter even when zero useful work happened. Result: cells where the provider was completely unreachable end up with turns=6 (5 retries), output_tokens=0, terminated_mid_work=nil, but `matrixHasMeaningfulAttempt(report)` returns true because turns \u0026gt; 0 — bypassing the new invalid_provider classifier rule introduced in 6688326e (fizeau-e874633d).\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Concrete incident: on 2026-05-11 ~15:25Z, vidar:1235 oMLX server crashed. 70 cells silently failed before detection. fiz.txt showed:\u0026#xA;  2026/05/11 15:29:41 WARN provider error, retrying attempt=1 err=\u0026#34;unexpected EOF\u0026#34;\u0026#xA;  2026/05/11 15:29:42 WARN provider error, retrying attempt=2 err=\u0026#34;connect: connection refused\u0026#34;\u0026#xA;  ... etc through attempt=5\u0026#xA;Each cell ended with turns=6, wall=60-200s, final_status=graded_fail. Classifier left them as plain graded_fail — i.e. \u0026#34;the model attempted and failed\u0026#34; — polluting vidar\u0026#39;s pass-rate denominator with what was actually 100% provider unavailability.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;The hole is structural: hasMeaningfulAttempt currently looks at turns/tokens/tool_calls \u0026gt; 0. fiz\u0026#39;s retry counter is one of the inputs to that signal, but a retry isn\u0026#39;t a meaningful attempt — it\u0026#39;s the absence of one.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;PROPOSED FIX\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Add a stronger \u0026#34;no real attempt\u0026#34; signal that distinguishes retry-spam from real turns. Two complementary options:\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;A. **fiz records retry attempts separately** from successful llm.request/response pairs. The session jsonl would carry an `llm.retry` event (or annotate llm.request with an `attempt` field). The matrix runner already reads the session jsonl in readSessionSignalsFromCell — it can extend the count to distinguish \u0026#34;had_completed_response\u0026#34; from \u0026#34;had_request\u0026#34;. Then: graded_fail + !had_completed_response + had_request → invalid_provider, regardless of turns count.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;B. **Token-based fallback in the existing classifier**: even if turns \u0026gt; 0, if input_tokens=0 AND output_tokens=0 AND had_llm_request=true AND tmw=nil, classify as invalid_provider. The intuition: a real turn consumes prompt tokens (input_tokens \u0026gt; 0 from session.end usage). All-zero token counts means no completed round-trip ever happened. Cheaper than (A) but a bit more heuristic.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;In-scope files for Part B (simpler, ships first):\u0026#xA;- cmd/bench/matrix_invalid.go — extend the case \u0026#34;graded_fail\u0026#34; branch with the token-based check before the !hasAttempt branch.\u0026#xA;- cmd/bench/matrix_invalid_test.go — fixture: graded-fail-retry-spam.json with turns=6, input_tokens=0, output_tokens=0, had_llm_request=true, tmw=nil → expects invalid_provider.\u0026#xA;- scripts/benchmark/reclassify-invalid.py — mirror.\u0026#xA;- Run reclassifier; expect ~70+ historical vidar cells from 2026-05-11 to flip invalid_setup/empty → invalid_provider.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;In-scope for Part A (deeper, file as separate bead if simple fix isn\u0026#39;t enough):\u0026#xA;- internal/core/loop.go — distinguish \u0026#34;request attempted but provider error retried\u0026#34; from \u0026#34;completed request/response pair\u0026#34; in event emission. Add an `attempt` field on llm.request or a new event type.\u0026#xA;- scripts/benchmark/harbor_agent.py FizeauAgent.parse_telemetry — count completed responses (not just requests) when populating turns/tokens fields.\u0026#xA;- cmd/bench/matrix.go readSessionSignalsFromCell — return n_completed_responses alongside the existing tmw/had_llm_request signals.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;ACCEPTANCE IS A COMMAND\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;1. go test ./cmd/bench/... -run TestClassifyMatrixInvalid passes with the new fixture graded-fail-retry-spam.json asserting invalid_provider.\u0026#xA;2. .venv-report/bin/python scripts/benchmark/reclassify-invalid.py --dry-run flags the cells from the 2026-05-11 vidar incident (70+ cells) as transitioning to invalid_provider.\u0026#xA;3. Apply pass leaves those cells excluded from vidar\u0026#39;s pass-rate denominator and tagged for --retry-invalid reruns.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;WHY THIS MATTERS\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Without this, every server-side outage (oMLX crash, vLLM hang, network blip) gets attributed to model quality instead of provider availability. Pass@k denominators include hundreds of cells where the model never actually got to try. The defense-in-depth piece (fizeau-72d18004 consecutive-failure halt in the matrix runner) catches this at sweep-execution time, but classification matters even retroactively for accurate reporting.\n    \u003c/description\u003e\n    \u003cacceptance\u003e\n1. New fixture graded-fail-retry-spam.json + test asserts invalid_provider on turns=6 + input_tokens=0 + output_tokens=0 + had_llm_request=true + tmw=nil. 2. reclassify-invalid.py --dry-run flags the 70+ historical vidar 2026-05-11 cells as transitioning to invalid_provider. 3. After apply, those cells are excluded from vidar\u0026#39;s pass-rate denominator. 4. Subsequent sweep with --retry-invalid re-runs them when the endpoint is back up.\n    \u003c/acceptance\u003e\n    \u003clabels\u003earea:benchmark, kind:reliability, kind:classifier\u003c/labels\u003e\n    \u003cmetadata parent=\"fizeau-1a5353cd\" base-rev=\"2ccf0ff9dc847cf06f56845b8f10571e12c4daa5\" bundle=\".ddx/executions/20260511T165929-b50938c3\"/\u003e\n  \u003c/bead\u003e\n  \u003cgoverning\u003e\n    \u003cnote\u003eNo governing references were pre-resolved. The bead description above is the primary contract. If it names files, specs, or prior beads, read those before editing. Ground decisions in what is already in the repository; do not guess.\u003c/note\u003e\n  \u003c/governing\u003e\n\u003c/execute-bead\u003e\n","metadata":{"DDX_MODE":"bead_execution","attempt_id":"20260511T165929-b50938c3","base_rev":"2ccf0ff9dc847cf06f56845b8f10571e12c4daa5","bead_id":"fizeau-25c4aea8","bundle_path":".ddx/executions/20260511T165929-b50938c3","correlation_id":"fizeau-25c4aea8:20260511T165929-b50938c3","prompt_file":".ddx/executions/20260511T165929-b50938c3/prompt.md","prompt_sha":"3b6bc8f755cb049114b0b693fd6587207227a6a8492c7ee04cb5044854c371b8","role":"implementer","session_id":"eb-e6a6d72f","worker_id":""}}}
